From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: intelxe-build <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:07:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] clang: SPIR-V builtins take int64_t, not the first 64-bit
 type

The SPIR-V builtin declarations used getIntTypeForBitwidth(64), the first
64-bit integer type: long. The SYCL headers convert 64-bit arguments to
[u]int64_t, which a SYCL device target takes from the host. On Linux both
are long, on Windows both long long; on a Darwin host int64_t is long long
while long is also 64-bit, so every 64-bit builtin call was ambiguous
(__spirv_ocl_nan, __spirv_GroupIAdd, ...). The 64-bit types are now the
target's Int64Type, so Linux and Windows are unchanged.
---
 clang/lib/Sema/SPIRVBuiltins.td | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/clang/lib/Sema/SPIRVBuiltins.td b/clang/lib/Sema/SPIRVBuiltins.td
index e5019b520..1630e76cf 100644
--- a/clang/lib/Sema/SPIRVBuiltins.td
+++ b/clang/lib/Sema/SPIRVBuiltins.td
@@ -328,8 +328,12 @@ def Short     : IntType<"short",     QualType<"Context.ShortTy", 0, 1>, 16>;
 def UShort    : UIntType<"ushort",    QualType<"Context.UnsignedShortTy">, 16>;
 def Int       : IntType<"int",       QualType<"Context.IntTy", 0, 1>, 32>;
 def UInt      : UIntType<"uint",      QualType<"Context.UnsignedIntTy">, 32>;
-def Long      : IntType<"long",      QualType<"Context.getIntTypeForBitwidth(64, true)", 0, 1>, 64>;
-def ULong     : UIntType<"ulong",     QualType<"Context.getIntTypeForBitwidth(64, false)">, 64>;
+// The 64-bit integers are the target's int64_t/uint64_t (Int64Type, which a
+// SYCL device target takes from the host): the SYCL headers pass
+// [u]int64_t. The first 64-bit type would be long on a Darwin host, where
+// int64_t is long long, and every 64-bit call would be ambiguous.
+def Long      : IntType<"long",      QualType<"(Context.getTargetInfo().getInt64Type() == TargetInfo::SignedLongLong ? Context.LongLongTy : Context.LongTy)", 0, 1>, 64>;
+def ULong     : UIntType<"ulong",     QualType<"(Context.getTargetInfo().getInt64Type() == TargetInfo::SignedLongLong ? Context.UnsignedLongLongTy : Context.UnsignedLongTy)">, 64>;
 def Float     : FPType<"float",     QualType<"Context.FloatTy">, 32>;
 def Double    : FPType<"double",    QualType<"Context.DoubleTy">, 64>;
 def Half      : FPType<"half",      QualTypeFromFunction<"GetFloat16Type">, 16>;
